## 5. Vente monorepo (add-on policy)

- **Packages:** `venteweb` (NestJS API), `vente-mobile` (Ionic/Angular/Capacitor), `ventewebf` (Angular web). **Experimental/alternate client:** `vente-mobile-flutter` (see its `AGENTS.md` when working there).
- **Source of truth:** `.codex-orchestration/project-context.md` (architecture, run commands, constraints, product narrative, **Run & Verify**). Keep it the canonical reference; do not replace it with guesses.
- **Mobile roadmap / phases:** `.codex-orchestration/mobile-roadmap.md` (phases, decisions, backlog).
- **Per-package guides:** `venteweb/AGENTS.md`, `ventewebf/AGENTS.md`, `vente-mobile/AGENTS.md`, `vente-mobile-flutter/AGENTS.md`, plus each package `README.md` as needed.
- **Language:** code, comments, and commit messages in **English**.

### Product priority (align with `project-context.md`)

- **MOBILE APP FIRST:** primary target is a **closed Android MVP** in `vente-mobile`; **iOS** is after that milestone. Scope should still express product values.
- **Backend (`venteweb`) and web (`ventewebf`)** back the mobile client: **API stability**, **DTO alignment** with mobile, and **small, targeted** web fixes. **Avoid** large web-only refactors unless explicitly scoped (e.g. Planner/orchestration).

### Codex orchestration (when using multi-agent handoffs)

- **Roles (only):** Planner, Coder, Verifier, Tester — see `.codex-orchestration/agents/*.md`.
- **Handoffs and reports:** `.codex-orchestration/handoffs/` (`planner-handoff.md`, `coder-notes.md`, `verifier-report.md`, `tester-report.md`).
- **Bootstrap:** `codex-bootstrap.ps1` (repo root) scaffolds the orchestration workspace; after changes, keep `project-context.md` and agent contexts aligned with the monorepo.

### Tools: RTK, MCP, Cursor hooks

- **RTK (Rust Token Killer):** [rtk-ai/rtk](https://github.com/rtk-ai/rtk). Prefer **`rtk`-prefixed** shell for noisy output (`rtk git status`, `rtk npm test`, etc.). In this repo: `RTK.md` (root; Codex) and the global **Cursor** hook (`%USERPROFILE%\.cursor\hooks.json` → `rtk hook cursor`) when the agent runs shell through the path that the hook rewrites. See **Run & Verify** in `project-context.md` for install/PATH. On native Windows, explicit `rtk` is still recommended for verbose commands; full hook parity is best in **WSL**.

- **MCP (Model Context Protocol):**  
  - **Codex CLI (this repo):** `.codex/config.toml` (e.g. `playwright`, `mobile_next` with explicit `npx` paths).  
  - **Cursor:** `.cursor/mcp.json` in the repo (merge with your user-level MCP config; Cursor may combine them). **Capability notes** for agents: `.codex-orchestration/mcp-browser-capability.md`, `.codex-orchestration/mcp-mobile-next-capability.md`.  
  - **Angular (`vente-mobile`, `ventewebf`):** Prefer MCP **`user-angular-cli`** for documentation and examples (`search_documentation`, `find_examples`, `get_best_practices`, `list_projects`) instead of ad‑hoc browsing of angular.dev alone; see each package `AGENTS.md`.
  - Use MCP tools that match the task (e.g. browser or device automation readmes under `.codex-orchestration/testing/` when relevant).

- **Project testing assets:** `.codex-orchestration/testing/` (e.g. Postman/Thunder collections, seed scripts, QA notes). Follow paths referenced from `project-context.md`.

### “Test myself” / APK (physical phone)

**Default:** global policy — emulator first; see Cursor **User Rules** (`%USERPROFILE%\.cursor\USER_RULES_ANDROID_TESTING.md`) or `~\.codex\AGENTS.md` (Codex CLI). When the **physical device** path applies **in Vente**, use **`.cursor/rules/mobile-self-test-apk.mdc`** + **`.codex-orchestration/testing/mobile-apk-self-test.md`** (Postgres + `venteweb`, build/sync/APK path, paths and network for the phone).

### Build / dev (policy)

- **Do not** run production **`build`** unless new dependencies (or explicit bootstrap) require it. Prefer: `npm run start:dev` (`venteweb`), `ionic cap run android` or `npm run android:live` (`vente-mobile` per `README`), `ng s` (`ventewebf`). Details: `project-context.md` → **Run & Verify** and **Constraints**.

### When project rules and Karpathy seem to conflict

The four principles in sections **1–4** are the behavioral baseline. Vente “do / don’t” in section **5** and in `project-context.md` **constrains domain and process** (e.g. DTOs, API stability, which directory to use); they are **not** an excuse to skip surgical editing, simplicity, or verifiable success criteria.
